From: build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0025] spot becomes a corpus, and the health check stops crying wolf

TWO THINGS, BOTH FOUND BY RUNNING 0024 AGAINST REFRESHED DATA.

A. SPOT WAS A CACHE, NOT A CORPUS
fetch_binance_klines REWRITES the whole spot file every run. Three consecutive
runs against unchanged history produced three different digests:

    0c013cfeb290b5bf -> 315ef254024a1818 -> 8ef481aa3298771c

Same days, different bytes, because the last row is TODAY and its OHLC moves
every time you ask. The spot series had no append-only guarantee, no prefix
hash, and no reproducibility. The linear and funding corpora have had all three
since slice 60; spot never did, because until 0020 it was Bitstamp and nothing
important read it. It is now HALF THE BASIS.

 + tools/append_spot_corpus.py   appends ONLY days after the current last row.
                                 Two distinct refusals: TODAY has not closed, so
                                 its bar is an in-progress quote wearing a
                                 close's clothes; a day ALREADY PRESENT must not
                                 be rewritten even if the venue now reports it
                                 differently, because a corpus that updates its
                                 own past is a cache.
                                 Verifies the old bytes are a byte-prefix of the
                                 new file, and verifies what actually LANDED on
                                 disk rather than what it meant to write.
                                 Restores from backup and exits non-zero on
                                 either failure. Dry-run by default.

B. THE HEALTH CHECK WAS WRONG THREE WAYS
0024 flagged a correctly-refreshed corpus as unhealthy. A check that cries wolf
gets ignored, which is worse than no check.

  1. OPEN BAR ON FUNDING - a category error. A funding print is an INSTANTANEOUS
     SETTLED EVENT: the 00:00 print today is as final as the 00:00 print last
     year and has no open state to be in. Bars have one; events do not. Now
     applied to per_day == 1 series only.

  2. INCOMPLETE FIRST DAY - the corpus BEGINS mid-day, so the first day has
     fewer than three prints by construction. Neither edge day is judged now:
     the first because it is partial, the last because it is still running.
     Flagging either marks every correct series unhealthy forever.

  3. COVERAGE DIFFERENCE REPORTED AS A HOLE - spot begins 2022-09-10 and perp
     begins 2022-08-10. Those 31 days are PERMANENT and no refresh will ever
     close them. A day missing from the MIDDLE of another series is a hole and a
     bug; a day outside its range is neither. Now reported separately, and the
     word "defect" is only used for the first.

  The remaining INCOMPLETE_DAYS flag at an INTERIOR date survives all three
  fixes and is a genuine funding gap worth investigating.

 + tests/test_append_spot_corpus.py   11 tests, including that a SECOND
                                 identical run leaves the digest unchanged -
                                 which is precisely the property the old
                                 fetcher lacked.

VERIFIED: 5,333 passed, 2 skipped (was 5,322). Fixture md5 stable.

